{"meta":{"title":"Knowing and Living the Self","subtitle":"An anonymous survey of adults aged 18–50 in Rwanda","data_file":"KoBoToolbox API (live)","source":"kobo","built":"2026-11-20T15:59:44Z","n_all":20,"n_valid":18},"themes":[{"key":"identity","label":"Who I am","items":["q6","q7","q8","q9","q10"]},{"key":"social","label":"Myself among others","items":["q11","q12","q13","q14","q15"]},{"key":"feedback","label":"Strengths, criticism and mistakes","items":["q16","q17","q18","q19","q20"]},{"key":"values","label":"Values and actions","items":["q21","q22","q23"]},{"key":"reflect","label":"Emotions and reflection","items":["q24","q25","q26"]}],"items":[{"key":"q6","num":6,"short":"Hard to describe myself beyond roles or achievements","theme":"identity","reverse":true},{"key":"q7","num":7,"short":"Unsure what would remain if I lost an important role","theme":"identity","reverse":true},{"key":"q8","num":8,"short":"Self-understanding changes with what others say","theme":"identity","reverse":true},{"key":"q9","num":9,"short":"Wonder if I truly wanted a decision or followed expectations","theme":"identity","reverse":true},{"key":"q10","num":10,"short":"Recognise what makes me different without ranking myself","theme":"identity","reverse":false},{"key":"q11","num":11,"short":"Present very different versions of myself across groups","theme":"social","reverse":true},{"key":"q12","num":12,"short":"Copy others to feel accepted","theme":"social","reverse":true},{"key":"q13","num":13,"short":"What I say I want changes with who I talk to","theme":"social","reverse":true},{"key":"q14","num":14,"short":"Made important choices to avoid disappointing someone","theme":"social","reverse":true},{"key":"q15","num":15,"short":"Know which beliefs are my own even when unpopular","theme":"social","reverse":false},{"key":"q16","num":16,"short":"Identify my strengths and limitations without help","theme":"feedback","reverse":false},{"key":"q17","num":17,"short":"First reaction to criticism is to defend myself","theme":"feedback","reverse":true},{"key":"q18","num":18,"short":"Try to appear strong even when struggling","theme":"feedback","reverse":true},{"key":"q19","num":19,"short":"Pause and examine an unfamiliar description of me","theme":"feedback","reverse":false},{"key":"q20","num":20,"short":"Admit I was wrong without being defined by it","theme":"feedback","reverse":false},{"key":"q21","num":21,"short":"Can name and explain my guiding values","theme":"values","reverse":false},{"key":"q22","num":22,"short":"Recent actions reflect my stated values","theme":"values","reverse":false},{"key":"q23","num":23,"short":"Recognise when behaviour goes against my values","theme":"values","reverse":false},{"key":"q24","num":24,"short":"Identify what triggered a strong emotion","theme":"reflect","reverse":false},{"key":"q25","num":25,"short":"Make time to examine choices and patterns","theme":"reflect","reverse":false},{"key":"q26","num":26,"short":"Know if an argument protects values or pride","theme":"reflect","reverse":false}],"statements":{"q6":"When someone asks me to describe who I am, I find it difficult to know what to say beyond my roles, responsibilities, or achievements.","q7":"When I imagine losing an important role, such as my job, relationship, or position in the family, I am unsure what would remain of my identity.","q8":"My understanding of who I am changes considerably depending on what other people say or think about me.","q9":"After making an important decision, I sometimes wonder, “Did I genuinely want this, or was I influenced by what others expected?”","q10":"I can recognise the qualities that make me different from people around me without needing to see myself as better or worse than them.","q11":"I notice that I present very different versions of myself depending on whether I am with family, friends, colleagues, or other groups.","q12":"I sometimes copy how other people speak, dress, behave, or express opinions because I want to feel accepted.","q13":"What I say I want can change depending on who I am talking to at the time.","q14":"I have made important choices in relationships, work, or life mainly because I did not want to disappoint someone.","q15":"Even when my opinion is unpopular, I can recognise which thoughts and beliefs are genuinely my own.","q16":"I can identify my strengths and limitations without needing someone else to point them out first.","q17":"When someone criticises me, my first reaction is usually to defend myself rather than consider whether the criticism may be useful.","q18":"I try to appear strong and in control, even when I am struggling, uncertain, or in need of help.","q19":"When someone describes me in a way I do not recognise, I can pause and examine their perspective before accepting or rejecting it.","q20":"I can admit that I was wrong without feeling that the mistake defines who I am.","q21":"I can name the personal values that guide my decisions and explain why those values matter to me.","q22":"Looking back at my recent choices, my actions generally reflect the values I say are important to me.","q23":"When my behaviour goes against my values, I can recognise the inconsistency instead of immediately justifying it.","q24":"I can usually identify what triggered a strong emotion, such as anger, frustration, fear, jealousy, excitement, or happiness.","q25":"I intentionally make time to examine my choices, emotions, and recurring patterns, even when no one else will know that I have done so.","q26":"When I am in an argument, I can easily know if it is to protect my values or to protect my pride."},"activity_options":["Studying","Employed full-time","Employed part-time","Self-employed / running a business","Unemployed, looking for work","Working mother","Stay-at-home mother","Working father","Stay-at-home father","More than one applies equally","Other"],"circumstance_options":["Single","Dating / in a relationship","Married","Separated, divorced or widowed","Parent","Sign